34
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:35,720
Language Takeaway.

35
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:44,030
Okay so Marco, a lot of the conversation today was about markets and a target consumer.

36
00:02:44,490 --> 00:02:51,630
So perhaps we should start talking a little bit about who Mr. Ford thinks this company's consumers are.

37
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:52,610
That's right.

38
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:57,830
He mentioned that the Alpha laptop could also be aimed at the middle class.

39
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:10,360
We have different classes in society, especially in America, where we talk about people who are low income, they don't make very much money, or people who make a lot of money, they're rich, they're on top.

40
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:11,860
That's the high class.

41
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:12,640
Yeah, high class.

42
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:14,420
But in the middle, we have the middle class.

43
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:15,880
And this is just average people.

44
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,220
They make money, they have a car.

45
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:19,360
They're not rich, but they're not poor.

46
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:20,960
Okay so they're in the middle.

47
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,800
So this is the middle class.

48
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:30,590
The computer is aimed at the middle class market, but he said that it's middle class white collar worker.

49
00:03:31,590 --> 00:03:40,830
Okay so I know this phrase exists in many other languages, but a white collar worker in English means, refers to the color of the shirt that you wear.

50
00:03:41,670 --> 00:03:43,950
So white collar workers usually work in offices.

51
00:03:44,410 --> 00:03:45,810
So because they're usually wearing suits.

52
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:49,690
That's right, they have to wear nice clothes like suits and button down shirts.

53
00:03:50,010 --> 00:03:52,590
But we sometimes also talk about blue collar workers.

54
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:53,230
Who are these guys?

55
00:03:54,470 --> 00:04:04,870
Blue collar workers are usually people that are in trades, like for example a mechanic or a plumber, because usually you see them wearing those blue shirts.

56
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:05,810
Yeah, uniforms.

57
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:11,820
They're usually people who work with their hands or who are not likely to work in a big office.

58
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:15,470
So usually maybe these people are not middle class, maybe they are lower class.

59
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:16,530
They can be both.

60
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:21,650
In America right now I think you can make quite a bit of money if you're a plumber or construction worker.

61
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:22,490
That's right.

62
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:30,240
But he also mentioned middle class white collar worker with an above average income.

63
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:35,780
Okay so an income is the amount of money that a person earns, usually in a year.

64
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,260
So we say $30,000 a year.

65
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:39,500
That's your annual income.

66
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,920
That's right.

67
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:43,040
So when we talk about something that's average, that means it's normal.

68
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,900
But in this case we're not talking about something that's average.

69
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:46,740
What are we talking about?

70
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:47,860
It's above average.

71
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:48,780
Above average.

72
00:04:49,500 --> 00:05:00,270
So if the average income of a person in America is $36,000 a year, an above average income is $70,000 a year or $65,000 a year.

73
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:02,510
But for the middle class maybe that's different.

74
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:06,740
So in the middle class an average annual income is $70,000.

75
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:11,700
An above average income in the middle class is $120,000 a year.

76
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:18,200
So the phrase there above average, you're just referring to something that's more than the normal.

77
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:18,330
That's right.

78
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:22,230
So in this case more than the normal income for a middle class worker.

79
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,510
You can also say below average.

80
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:29,970
So a below average income is lower than most people earn.

81
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:30,590
Okay.

82
00:05:30,850 --> 00:05:31,250
Very good.

83
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:40,230
And well continuing on talking about markets and the demographics, who were selling the computer to, we also talked about our target consumer.

84
00:05:41,030 --> 00:05:44,950
This is something that you often hear in meetings at work or in marketing departments.

85
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:47,850
A target is something you aim for.

86
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:50,370
It's something you want to hit or achieve.

87
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:57,700
And so a target consumer is the buyer, is a customer that you aim to have.

88
00:05:57,910 --> 00:05:58,190
Okay.

89
00:05:58,350 --> 00:06:07,250
So maybe you have some customers that they're students and you have some customers that they're very old, but your target consumer are the people that you really want to reach out to.

90
00:06:08,210 --> 00:06:11,830
In this case, the middle class white collar worker.

91
00:06:12,130 --> 00:06:12,530
That's right.

92
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:19,910
So in the case of our dialogue, our target consumer is a middle class white collar worker, for example.

93
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,540
Okay.

94
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:26,410
So a lot of marketing stuff here talking about the computer and what Mr. Ford was saying.

